  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Points \\(A(11, 9)\\) and \\(B(2, -3)\\) are vertices of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) with \\(AB=AC.\\) The altitude from \\(A\\) meets the opposite side at \\(D(-1, 3).\\) What are the coordinates of point \\(C?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\((-8, 9) \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\((-4, 8) \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\((-4, 9) \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\((-2, 3) \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\((-1, 0) \\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2017-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(AB=AC,\\) the altitude from \\(A\\) also bisects the base \\(BC.\\) Therefore, \\(D\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC.\\) If \\(C=(x,y),\\) then we have \\[\\frac{x+2}2 = -1,\\]\\[\\frac{y-3}2=3.\\] As such, \\[C=(x,y)=(-4,9).\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "In an isosceles triangle, the altitude from the vertex also bisects the base",
        "Use \\(D\\) as the midpoint of \\(BC\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
